WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.236 --> 00:00:01.673
- Good morning Believe Nation,

00:00:01.673 --> 00:00:05.779
today's message is define
happiness for yourself.

00:00:05.779 --> 00:00:07.945
Over to you, Alfred Hitchcock.

00:00:07.945 --> 00:00:10.172
(rooster crows)

00:00:10.172 --> 00:00:12.763
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:12.763 --> 00:00:15.518
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:15.518 --> 00:00:19.731
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:19.731 --> 00:00:23.898
- Mr. Hitchcock, what is
your definition of happiness?

00:00:25.486 --> 00:00:26.986
- A clear horizon,

00:00:28.375 --> 00:00:31.375
nothing to worry about on your plate

00:00:32.971 --> 00:00:37.138
only things that are
creative and not destructive,

00:00:41.655 --> 00:00:43.455
and that's within yourself.

00:00:43.455 --> 00:00:44.288
Within me,

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:49.987
I can't bear quarreling.

00:00:49.987 --> 00:00:53.649
I can't bear feelings between people.

00:00:53.649 --> 00:00:56.232
I think hatred is wasted energy

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:00.591
and it's all non-productive.

00:01:01.623 --> 00:01:04.035
I'm very sensitive.

00:01:04.035 --> 00:01:08.202
A sharp word said by, say,
a person who has a temper

00:01:11.218 --> 00:01:13.402
if they're close to me,

00:01:13.402 --> 00:01:15.573
hurts me for days.

00:01:15.573 --> 00:01:17.747
I know we're only human,

00:01:17.747 --> 00:01:20.997
we do go in for these various emotions,

00:01:22.342 --> 00:01:24.675
call them negative emotions,

00:01:25.517 --> 00:01:28.122
but when all these are removed

00:01:28.122 --> 00:01:32.660
and you can look forward
and the road is clear ahead

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.754
and now you're going to create something,

00:01:35.754 --> 00:01:39.934
I think that's as happy as
I would ever want to be.

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:42.275
- I think this is one of
the most important exercises

00:01:42.275 --> 00:01:44.441
that you can do, not
just as an entrepreneur,

00:01:44.441 --> 00:01:45.819
but as a human being.

00:01:45.819 --> 00:01:49.302
To understand what
happiness looks like for you

00:01:49.302 --> 00:01:52.392
so that you can build
a life and a business

00:01:52.392 --> 00:01:53.944
that makes you happier.

00:01:53.944 --> 00:01:55.403
Self- awareness is important.

00:01:55.403 --> 00:01:57.426
It's why I wrote the book, Your One Word.

00:01:57.426 --> 00:02:01.188
To understand what is the thing
that makes you come alive.

00:02:01.188 --> 00:02:03.489
Understanding that,
understanding what you're one

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:06.156
main core value is that you love

00:02:07.857 --> 00:02:11.322
and then being proactive
and going after that.

00:02:11.322 --> 00:02:13.166
In the book, we go through that exercise

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:14.397
of thinking about everything

00:02:14.397 --> 00:02:16.246
that has made you come alive in the past.

00:02:16.246 --> 00:02:17.457
What makes you happy?

00:02:17.457 --> 00:02:19.829
Make a list of all the
things that make you happy.

00:02:19.829 --> 00:02:22.462
The movies you watch and
the people in your life

00:02:22.462 --> 00:02:24.027
and what you loved about your parents

00:02:24.027 --> 00:02:25.810
and whoever your favorite teacher was.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.943
Of the hundreds of teachers that you had,

00:02:27.943 --> 00:02:30.147
the one or two people that stood out,

00:02:30.147 --> 00:02:31.666
what was it about them?

00:02:31.666 --> 00:02:33.647
What were the highest highs in your life?

00:02:33.647 --> 00:02:35.072
What were you doing?

00:02:35.072 --> 00:02:38.756
What are the activities
that make you come alive?

00:02:38.756 --> 00:02:41.269
To build a happy life,
you want to be around that

00:02:41.269 --> 00:02:42.626
as much as possible.

00:02:42.626 --> 00:02:44.783
You want to be doing things
that make you come alive, right?

00:02:44.783 --> 00:02:47.362
Who wants a life that is boring?

00:02:47.362 --> 00:02:50.065
That you're doing stuff
that is just repetitive

00:02:50.065 --> 00:02:52.780
and beneath you consistently.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.396
Nobody wants that life.

00:02:54.396 --> 00:02:58.948
But doing the things that
create the spark for you,

00:02:58.948 --> 00:03:02.123
that add tons of value
to other people's lives,

00:03:02.123 --> 00:03:04.011
that give you that proud feeling

00:03:04.011 --> 00:03:06.408
of the work that you're
doing is contributing,

00:03:06.408 --> 00:03:07.943
that's what you want to get to.

00:03:07.943 --> 00:03:10.780
Making that list of the things
that make you come alive

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:13.256
and finding what's the
common theme between

00:03:13.256 --> 00:03:14.185
all of those things.

00:03:14.185 --> 00:03:15.845
For me, it's belief.

00:03:15.845 --> 00:03:18.402
I've talked about my
favorite movie is Seabiscuit.

00:03:18.402 --> 00:03:21.668
It's about this undersized
horse and oversized jockey,

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.964
an owner that had no money,

00:03:23.964 --> 00:03:25.683
that everybody was counting out

00:03:25.683 --> 00:03:27.760
and somehow those three guys came together

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:30.093
and they won a ton of races.

00:03:31.346 --> 00:03:36.064
They beat all the odds, that
underdog story of believe.

00:03:36.064 --> 00:03:37.896
My parents told me I was
a Gastrilli Carmichael,

00:03:37.896 --> 00:03:40.947
I could do anything I wanted, is believe.

00:03:40.947 --> 00:03:42.810
My favorite teachers were about believe.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:45.635
The people that I want
to surround myself with

00:03:45.635 --> 00:03:46.808
need to be about believe.

00:03:46.808 --> 00:03:48.869
Why it's so important
is 'cause understanding

00:03:48.869 --> 00:03:53.649
what value is so important
to me, and was in the past,

00:03:53.649 --> 00:03:56.183
now let's me build a future that's better.

00:03:56.183 --> 00:03:58.319
So, I can build a business around believe.

00:03:58.319 --> 00:04:01.968
I can bring teammates on
board who believe in believe.

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:03.343
I can be more proactive.

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:06.060
Instead of having life
happen to me by accident

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:07.690
or instead of, even worse,

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:09.685
having other people's projections

00:04:09.685 --> 00:04:12.438
of what I should do, impact me.

00:04:12.438 --> 00:04:14.525
If you don't know what you stand for

00:04:14.525 --> 00:04:16.440
you will fall for anything.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:17.704
You'll just be walking around living

00:04:17.704 --> 00:04:19.497
up to other people's expectations

00:04:19.497 --> 00:04:21.780
instead of doing the
thing that you want to do.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.544
But, a lot of people
don't have the clarity.

00:04:23.544 --> 00:04:25.152
A lot of people walk
through life feeling like

00:04:25.152 --> 00:04:27.207
they could be doing way more.

00:04:27.207 --> 00:04:29.419
You know that you could be doing way more

00:04:29.419 --> 00:04:31.548
in your life than you're
currently doing right now

00:04:31.548 --> 00:04:33.420
but you don't know what to do

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.842
because you're not clear
on what your value is.

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:37.305
You're not clear on what you stand for

00:04:37.305 --> 00:04:39.521
so you can't build that ideal life.

00:04:39.521 --> 00:04:42.878
In my view, I'm biased,
I wrote a book about it,

00:04:42.878 --> 00:04:45.742
but in my view it's one of the single

00:04:45.742 --> 00:04:48.134
most important exercises
that you can ever do

00:04:48.134 --> 00:04:50.403
in your life, whether you're
an entrepreneur or not.

00:04:50.403 --> 00:04:53.031
To understand what it
is that makes you happy.

00:04:53.031 --> 00:04:56.488
What you're most important
core value is for you

00:04:56.488 --> 00:04:59.535
has always been, always will be,

00:04:59.535 --> 00:05:03.819
and with design, with
intent, with purpose,

00:05:03.819 --> 00:05:06.756
building a life and a business around it

00:05:06.756 --> 00:05:09.608
that will make you happy forever.

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:12.298
Imagine that, it's possible.

00:05:12.298 --> 00:05:14.097
It's achievable

00:05:14.097 --> 00:05:15.684
and I want it for you.

00:05:15.684 --> 00:05:17.400
So, the question of the day today is

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:20.336
how do you define happiness for yourself?

00:05:20.336 --> 00:05:22.252
What is your one word?

00:05:22.252 --> 00:05:23.769
Leave it in the comments below.

00:05:23.769 --> 00:05:25.425
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:26.648
I also want to give a quick shout-out

00:05:26.648 --> 00:05:29.965
to Regina Ross from
ReginasBeautyBoutique.com.

00:05:29.965 --> 00:05:31.731
Thank you so much, Regina,
for picking up a copy

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:33.276
of my book, Your One Word.

00:05:33.276 --> 00:05:35.796
It really, really, really,
really means a lot to me.

00:05:35.796 --> 00:05:37.383
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:05:37.383 --> 00:05:38.476
I believe in you.

00:05:38.476 --> 00:05:40.607
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:05:40.607 --> 00:05:42.808
and whatever your one word is.

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:45.248
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:05:45.248 --> 00:05:47.767
for another shot of espresso.

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:50.424
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:50.424 --> 00:05:53.659
♫ Espresso keep me going

